-- title:
--   Theorem 2: convergence of EGRAAL for monotone VIs with locally Lipschitz $F$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal E$ be a finite-dimensional real inner product space and consider the variational inequality
--   $$\text{find } z^*\in\mathcal E\ \text{ such that }\ \langle F(z^*),z-z^*\rangle+g(z)-g(z^*)\ge0\quad\forall z\in\mathcal E. \tag{1}$$
--   Assume
--
--   1. (C1) the solution set $S$ of (1) is nonempty;
--   2. (C2) $g:\mathcal E\to(-\infty,+\infty]$ is proper, convex and lower semicontinuous;
--   3. (C3) $F$ is monotone on $\operatorname{dom} g$: $\langle F(u)-F(v),u-v\rangle\ge0$ for all $u,v\in\operatorname{dom} g$;
--   4. $F$ is locally Lipschitz continuous on $\operatorname{dom} g$.
--
--   Let $\varphi\in(1,\phi]$ with $\phi=\frac{1+\sqrt5}{2}$, $\lambda_0>0$, $\bar\lambda>0$, $z^0,z^1\in\mathcal E$, and let $(z^k),(\bar z^k)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (EGRAAL). Then there is $z^*\in S$ with
--   $$z^k\to z^*\qquad\text{and}\qquad \bar z^k\to z^* .$$
--
--   EGRAAL needs no Lipschitz constant and no linesearch: each step uses one evaluation of $F$ and one proximal step, and the stepsizes adapt to the local Lipschitz constant of $F$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: g : E → (−∞, +∞] proper convex lsc → a set D with real values g : E → ℝ; D nonempty, ConvexOn ℝ D g, and the extension by +∞ off D lower semicontinuous (IsProperConvexLsc); reason: every proper convex lsc g is of this form (D = dom g) and conversely; same instances
--   - generalization: F : dom g → E; inputs z⁰, z¹ at which F is evaluated in (15), (17) → F : E → E, with monotonicity (and local Lipschitz continuity, where assumed) imposed on D only and values off D unconstrained; z 0, z 1 ∈ E arbitrary; reason: specializes to the paper by taking z⁰, z¹ ∈ dom g and any extension of F off dom g; for k ≥ 2 the iterates lie in dom g
--   - encoding: convention 0/0 = +∞ in (15) → egraalStep omits the middle entry of the minimum when F(z^k) = F(z^{k−1}); reason: the middle entry is then a/0 with a ≥ 0, i.e. +∞, and drops out of the minimum; same stepsizes
--   - encoding: z^{k+1} = prox_{λ_k g}(z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) with prox a function → IsProx D (λ_k g) (z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) (z^{k+1}): z^{k+1} ∈ D minimizes λ_k g(x) + ½‖x − w‖² over D; reason: under (C2) in finite dimension the minimizer exists and is unique, so the predicate determines the same iterates
--   - reading: F is locally Lipschitz-continuous → LocallyLipschitzOn D F (every point of dom g has a neighbourhood within dom g on which F is Lipschitz); reason: F is defined only on dom g (C3), so local Lipschitz continuity is read on its domain; LocallyLipschitz F on all of E would add a hypothesis
--   - reading: (z^k) and (z̄^k) converge to a solution of (1) → there is one solution z∗ with z^k → z∗ and z̄^k → z∗; reason: the stronger of the two readings (a common limit); the proof gives ‖z^k − z̄^k‖ → 0
-- source:
--   Malitsky, Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities, preprint (2018), §2.1, p. 6, Theorem 2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsProperConvexLsc
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsMonotoneOn
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsVISolution
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsEGRAALRun

open Filter Topology

namespace GoldenRatioVI

/-- **Theorem 2: convergence of the Explicit Golden Ratio Algorithm (EGRAAL).**
Malitsky, *Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities*, preprint (2018), §2.1, p. 6, Theorem 2: "Suppose that F is locally Lipschitz-continuous and conditions
(C1)–(C3) are satisfied. Then (zk) and (z̄k), generated by Algorithm 1, converge to a solution of
(1)."

Let `E` be a finite-dimensional real inner product space, `g : E → (−∞, +∞]` proper convex lsc
(given by its domain `D` and finite values `g`), `F` monotone and locally Lipschitz on `dom g`, and
suppose (1) has a solution. For every `φ ∈ (1, ϕ]`, `λ₀ > 0`, `λ̄ > 0` and every run of Algorithm 1
(any `z⁰, z¹ ∈ E`), there is a solution `z∗` of (1) with `z^k → z∗` and `z̄^k → z∗`.

**Formalization Note.** Conventions: `g` is the pair `(D, g)`, lsc of the `+∞`-extension
(`IsProperConvexLsc`); `F : E → E` with (C3) and local Lipschitz continuity on `D` only, values off
`D` unconstrained; `z 0, z 1 ∈ E` arbitrary; the rule (15) uses `0/0 = +∞` (`egraalStep`); the prox
is a minimizer predicate (`IsProx`); both sequences converge to one common solution. `ϕ` is
`Real.goldenRatio`. -/
theorem theorem_2_egraal_converges {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {D : Set E} {g : E → ℝ} {F : E → E} {phi lam0 lbar : ℝ}
    {z zbar : ℕ → E} {lam theta : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hg : IsProperConvexLsc D g) (hF : IsMonotoneOn D F) (hS : ∃ zs, IsVISolution D g F zs)
    (hLip : LocallyLipschitzOn D F)
    (hphi : 1 < phi) (hphiG : phi ≤ Real.goldenRatio) (hlam0 : 0 < lam0) (hlbar : 0 < lbar)
    (hrun : IsEGRAALRun D g F phi lam0 lbar z zbar lam theta) :
    ∃ zs : E, IsVISolution D g F zs ∧ Tendsto z atTop (𝓝 zs) ∧ Tendsto zbar atTop (𝓝 zs) := by sorry

end GoldenRatioVI
